---
title: '"Think once" system'
publishedAt: 2026-11-17
draft: true
---
Thinking is hard. With the destructive use of technology, we're losing the ability to keep our the purpose of previous novel decisions when considering what to do next.

If that's not you, congratulations, your life is probably the best it can be.

I'm looking to design a way, at least in software development, to think once.

## 1. Write it down

Why remember when you don't have to?

Even better, imagine you could remember?

Writing it down means we can check later in case we do forget, and helps us remember.

It's a win win, no need to make a choice. If you write it down, you'll remember AND there's a reference when the choice gets real hard and reflection is required.

## 2. Picking the least worst

## 3. Dreams are for pipes

Do something achievable. If you can't get a plan together to do the thing, you're taking a big risk. All in or all out mostly.
